<title>USA: Welsh, Carson vies for CompuServe - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Welsh, Carson vies for CompuServe - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>New York investment firm Welsh, Carson, Anderson &amp; Stowe is said to be among the companies vying for CompuServe Corp, The Wall Street Journal said.</p>
<p>In Monday's electronic edition, the paper said the firm had joined others, including America Online Inc, in vying for the on-line service.</p>
<p>The story said the information came from Welsh, Carson executives.</p>
<p>H&amp;R Block is trying to sell its 80-percent stake in CompuServe and is holding out for better offers, the Journal said.</p>
<p>Welsh, Carson was not immediately available to comment.</p>
</text>
